  <keyword>fitrknn</keyword>
  <short_description>Fit a k-nearest-neighbor regression model.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>mdl = fitrknn(X, Y)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>mdl = fitrknn(X, Y, Name, Value)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>yfit = predict(mdl, Xnew)</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>[yfit, D] = predict(mdl, Xnew)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <description>
    <p><b>fitrknn</b> creates a <b>RegressionKNN</b> object from numeric predictors <b>X</b> and numeric response <b>Y</b>.</p>
    <p>Name-value arguments include <b>NumNeighbors</b>, <b>Distance</b>, <b>DistanceWeight</b>, <b>Standardize</b>, <b>P</b>, <b>Scale</b>, <b>PredictorNames</b>, and <b>ResponseName</b>. Prediction returns weighted neighbor response averages.</p>
  </description>
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[X = [0 0; 0 1; 1 0; 5 5; 5 6; 6 5];
Y = [1; 1.2; 1.1; 10; 10.2; 10.1];
mdl = fitrknn(X, Y, 'NumNeighbors', 3);
yfit = predict(mdl, [0.2 0.1; 5.2 5.1])]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
